* ''The memory stage's meme path'' (seat, talked out under the recipe and bags model, 2026-11-07; trued for the layers above working and by a Luna measure; overrulable). The daemon wiki's recipe reads, top to bottom, temp, draft, personal, working, the wiki's own canon bag, the kahua bag, the library bags and the oracle (`wiki-recipe.ts`), and a kāpae shadows downward only (`island-adaptor.ts`). (a) The stage law reads at the WORKING seam, where a meme becomes a stage meme: drafts and the other upper layers hold work in progress, so the stage's readers and `L11`'s index read working and canon, never drafts, and there a stage meme whose title disagrees with its key reads as a named fork, never a stage meme; the backstop writes its refusal as a diagnostic tiddler in the working bag beside its log line (owed on `L11` and the meme backstop). (b) Concurrency catches at the draft-to-working save: the native draft save carries the draft's captured Automerge heads as its base (`island-adaptor.ts`), a tiddler's text rests as one whole scalar (`stored-value.ts`), and `readParallelDrafts` surfaces concurrent values off Automerge's conflict set (`parallel-drafts.ts`), so a moved base keeps both sides visible and the stage's readers read through it; a write that skips a draft meets the same conflict read as its backstop (owed on `L11` and `L12` before multi-device dogfooding). (c) A burned stage meme raises a kāpae in the working bag, never a retract to absent (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae#/core-cut`>>), so it shadows a lower or re-poured copy; since a kāpae shadows downward only and drafts sync across a seated face's fleet (temp stays local), a burn also discards or shadows the open drafts and upper-layer copies of its meme; exports and re-pours carry the working layer and its kāpae records, never drafts. The disk projector writes a raised kāpae onto disk as `<stem>.kapae` and ingest raises it again, so a re-pour of an old export never brings a burned meme back (`L34` keeps the residues). (d) Two memories that choose one readable key settle by authoring discipline (`L19`'s class and slug) and `placeMeme`'s base-hash refusal, with no new mechanism. Stage memes stay in the kahua working projection under the kept state root (cleartext only on disk and in the live wiki), never pushed to git; durability past this machine rides the vault's backup door, as today's flat memories rest outside git.

